check_unresolved_imports {
    [check] reports an error when an import does not resolve.
    A missing import path is an error. A named imported idea that is not in the target file is an error.
    Do not report imported idea names when the path is missing.
    An existing folder is a valid import path ([import_folder_targets]).
    A remote URL is not a missing path.
    Import paths with no extension mean `.rq` first ([implicit_file_extension]).
    Ignore a site with [comment_reference_ignore].
    Issue kind is `import`. The `label` is the missing path or the missing idea name.
    Forms: [import_from], [import_namespace], [import_qualified].
    Editor underline: [import_does_not_exist_error].
    [check_skip_targets] matches that label. [check_skip_gitignored_targets] omits a missing import path that Git ignore rules ignore.
    Related: [check] [check_order_by_target] [import_does_not_exist_error]
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/check/imports.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/path_resolve.rs"]
        ["../../packages/cli/src/commands/check.ts"]
        ["../../packages/mcp/src/server.ts"]
        ["../../packages/extension/skills/rq-fix-stale-references/SKILL.md"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/broken_references.rs:check_reports_missing_import_path"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/broken_references.rs:check_reports_missing_imported_idea"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/broken_references.rs:check_accepts_resolved_imports"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/broken_references.rs:check_skips_import_on_rq_ignore_error"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/broken_references.rs:check_accepts_folder_and_implicit_extension_imports"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/broken_references.rs:check_skips_remote_import_urls"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/broken_references.rs:check_skips_gitignored_import_paths"]
        ["../../packages/cli/test/check.test.ts:reports unresolved imports and exits 1"]
    )
}

code_comment_syntax_errors {
    A comment reference uses `rq:[idea]` or `rq:["path".idea]`.
    A path string uses double quotes or single quotes.
    A qualified reference may use dotted idea names after the path.
    Line comments use `//` and `#`.
    The same forms apply in every comment span that the indexer reads.
    [check] reads each comment reference in a non-`.rq` source file.
    A comment reference with invalid syntax is a syntax error.
    [check] reports the syntax error.
    The issue kind is `comment_syntax`.
    The issue label is the error reason and the comment reference text.
    The issue severity is `error`.
    A valid comment reference stays a ["../language/syntax.rq".comment_reference] site.
    An unresolved valid target stays a `comment_link` issue.
    A source file that contains only a syntax error stays in the code index.
    [comment_reference_ignore] suppresses the syntax error on the next line.
    Related: [check] [check_rq_syntax] ["../extension/language/comment-references/functional-code-comment-references.rq".references_in_functional_code_comments]
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/comment.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/check/mod.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/sync.rs"]
        ["../../packages/cli/src/commands/check.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/comment.rs:reports_a_malformed_comment_reference"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/comment.rs:reports_an_unclosed_comment_reference"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/comment.rs:keeps_a_quoted_bracket_inside_a_qualified_comment_reference"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/comment.rs:ignores_malformed_rq_inside_strings_and_raw_strings"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/broken_references.rs:check_reports_a_malformed_comment_reference"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/broken_references.rs:check_skips_comment_syntax_on_rq_ignore_error"]
    )
}

check_rq_syntax {
    [check] reports a syntax error when an `.rq` file fails to parse.
    The parser (`reqlan-parse`) is the single source of the message and span.
    Example message: `expected idea, ideaset, or one-liner`.
    The language server already shows these diagnostics (["../extension/language/support/language-server-rust.rq".language_server_rust]).
    [check] must emit the same class of issue so CLI and CI catch what the editor underlines.
    Issue kind is `syntax`. The label is the parser message. Severity follows the parser diagnostic.
    A file that only fails to parse still appears in the issue list even when it contributes no ideas or references.
    [comment_reference_ignore] suppresses a syntax error on the next line (same rule as the language server).
    Comment-reference syntax in non-`.rq` files stays [code_comment_syntax_errors].
    Related: [check] [code_comment_syntax_errors] ["../core-architecture.rq".grammar_and_parser]
    @status pending
    @todo Surface `reqlan-parse` diagnostics through `check_references`; cover CLI/JSON and `//rq-ignore-error`.
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/src/parser.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/check/mod.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/sync.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-lsp/src/analysis.rs"]
        ["../../packages/cli/src/commands/check.ts"]
    )
}

check_meta_implementation {
    [check] is a step in the sequential GitHub CI job after one workspace build.
    Pull requests use ["../../.github/workflows/ci.yml"].
    Main uses the same workflow through ["../../.github/workflows/release.yml"] (["../distribution/distribution.rq".ci_gate]).
    The job installs workspace packages once (`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`), asserts `@reqlan/*` resolve under `packages/` (["../../scripts/assert-workspace-reqlan.mjs"]), compiles crates and TypeScript, then runs crate tests, `node packages/cli/bin/cli.js check`, and JS/TS tests against that build.
    Do not install `@reqlan/cli` or other `@reqlan/*` packages from npm. Platform natives in this workspace come from `packages/analytical-native/` via `packageExtensions` in ["../../pnpm-workspace.yaml"], not from the registry. Do not call a global `reqlan` binary. Do not run a second install before check.
    GitHub and Azure pass `--skip-gitignored-targets` because gitignored files are not in a CI checkout ([check_skip_gitignored_targets]).
    Azure uses the same workspace CLI after its package build on `ext/v*` tags.
    Related: [check] [check_skip_targets] [check_skip_gitignored_targets] ["../distribution/distribution.rq".ci_gate]
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../.github/workflows/ci.yml"]
        ["../../.github/workflows/release.yml"]
        ["../../azure-pipelines.yml"]
        ["../../package.json"]
        ["../../scripts/assert-workspace-reqlan.mjs"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/release-ci-gate.test.ts"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/release-ci-gate.test.ts:release calls sequential CI before versioning"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/release-ci-gate.test.ts:CI is one sequential pull-request job"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/release-ci-gate.test.ts:one build is reused by crate tests, check, and package tests"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/release-ci-gate.test.ts:reference check uses workspace packages not npm"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/release-ci-gate.test.ts:TypeScript compile generates Langium sources first"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/release-ci-gate.test.ts:CI check skips gitignored targets"]
    )
}
